   "text": "Functional requirements",
   "originalText": "Functional requirements",
   "fontSize": 30,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "el4_160816",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 26.0,
   "y": 214,
   "width": 580.32,
   "height": 382.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1953574603,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1089709947,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1795464137622,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Functional = what the system DOES.\nWrite each one as  \"<actor> can <verb> <object>\":\n\n• User can search / browse / filter items\n• User can add, update, remove things they own (cart, booking)\n• System creates objects of different TYPES or MODES\n   (delivery vs pickup, car vs bike, now vs scheduled)\n• System supports several WAYS to do one job\n   (payment modes, pricing rules, matching rules)\n• System notifies actors when something happens\n• Admin can manage the catalogue (add / update / remove)\n• Anyone can look up a record by id\n\nHow to collect them:\n1. List the actors (user, admin, system, external service)\n2. List the use cases per actor\n3. Keep the 5 to 8 core ones, write an \"Out of scope\" list",
   "originalText": "Functional = what the system DOES.\nWrite each one as  \"<actor> can <verb> <object>\":\n\n• User can search / browse / filter items\n• User can add, update, remove things they own (cart, booking)\n• System creates objects of different TYPES or MODES\n   (delivery vs pickup, car vs bike, now vs scheduled)\n• System supports several WAYS to do one job\n   (payment modes, pricing rules, matching rules)\n• System notifies actors when something happens\n• Admin can manage the catalogue (add / update / remove)\n• Anyone can look up a record by id\n\nHow to collect them:\n1. List the actors (user, admin, system, external service)\n2. List the use cases per actor\n3. Keep the 5 to 8 core ones, write an \"Out of scope\" list",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
