   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Non-functional requirements",
   "originalText": "Non-functional requirements",
   "fontSize": 30,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "el7_352353",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 936.0,
   "y": 214,
   "width": 636.48,
   "height": 337.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 194804717,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1183364968,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1795464137622,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Non-functional = how WELL it does it.\nName the quality, then the design choice that delivers it:\n\nExtensibility      → interfaces + Strategy / Factory\n                       (Open/Closed: add, don't edit)\nMaintainability    → one responsibility per class, folders by role\nLoose coupling     → client talks only to a Facade\nSingle source of truth → one Manager per collection (Singleton)\nConsistency        → change state only after the step succeeds\nScalability        → managers can later sit on a DB / service\nThread safety      → lock singletons, id generators, shared maps\nTestability        → depend on interfaces so fakes can be swapped in\n\nIn an LLD round, 4 or 5 of these are enough.\nLatency / availability are mostly HLD topics.",
   "originalText": "Non-functional = how WELL it does it.\nName the quality, then the design choice that delivers it:\n\nExtensibility      → interfaces + Strategy / Factory\n                       (Open/Closed: add, don't edit)\nMaintainability    → one responsibility per class, folders by role\nLoose coupling     → client talks only to a Facade\nSingle source of truth → one Manager per collection (Singleton)\nConsistency        → change state only after the step succeeds\nScalability        → managers can later sit on a DB / service\nThread safety      → lock singletons, id generators, shared maps\nTestability        → depend on interfaces so fakes can be swapped in\n\nIn an LLD round, 4 or 5 of these are enough.\nLatency / availability are mostly HLD topics.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
