   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Common LLD design patterns",
   "originalText": "Common LLD design patterns",
   "fontSize": 30,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "el10_334083",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1846.0,
   "y": 214,
   "width": 505.44,
   "height": 382.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1354258845,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1347402587,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1795464137622,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Singleton  →  exactly one shared instance\n     managers, registries, config, logger\nStrategy  →  swap an algorithm at runtime\n     payment modes, pricing, sorting, matching\nFactory  →  hide which subclass gets created\n     order / vehicle / notification types\nFacade  →  one simple entry point over many classes\n     the App / Controller class main.cpp talks to\nObserver  →  notify many listeners on an event\n     notifications, UI updates, subscriptions\nState  →  behaviour changes with the object's state\n     vending machine, elevator, order status\nDecorator  →  add features by wrapping an object\n     toppings, add-ons, logging wrappers\nBuilder  →  build objects with many optional fields\nAdapter  →  make an outside API fit your interface\nCommand  →  wrap a request as an object (undo, queues)",
   "originalText": "Singleton  →  exactly one shared instance\n     managers, registries, config, logger\nStrategy  →  swap an algorithm at runtime\n     payment modes, pricing, sorting, matching\nFactory  →  hide which subclass gets created\n     order / vehicle / notification types\nFacade  →  one simple entry point over many classes\n     the App / Controller class main.cpp talks to\nObserver  →  notify many listeners on an event\n     notifications, UI updates, subscriptions\nState  →  behaviour changes with the object's state\n     vending machine, elevator, order status\nDecorator  →  add features by wrapping an object\n     toppings, add-ons, logging wrappers\nBuilder  →  build objects with many optional fields\nAdapter  →  make an outside API fit your interface\nCommand  →  wrap a request as an object (undo, queues)",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
